Manage SSH authorized_keys across a fleet of servers

Usage:
  sshepherd [flags]
  sshepherd [command]

Available Commands:
  adopt       Generate a manifest that adopts every key already installed on the fleet
  apply       Make each server's authorized_keys match the manifest (writes to the fleet)
  audit       Report drift between the manifest and each server's authorized_keys (read-only)
  completion  Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  help        Help about any command
  import      Convert an OpenSSH client config into a starter manifest
  revoke      Remove users or keys from the manifest and push the change to the servers it affects
  rotate      Replace one of a user's keys in the manifest and push the swap to the servers it affects

Flags:
      --color string   colorize output: auto, always, or never (default "auto")
  -h, --help           help for sshepherd
  -q, --quiet          log errors only
  -v, --verbose        enable debug logging
      --version        version for sshepherd

Use "sshepherd [command] --help" for more information about a command.
